      "math_academy_id": "e-2756",
      "problem": "A regular pentagon has the same perimeter as an equilateral triangle whose side is $15\\,\\mathrm{cm}.$ Find the length of the side of the pentagon.",
      "worked_solution": "Since all the sides of an equilateral triangle are equal, its perimeter is \n\n$$\np=3\\cdot 15=45.\n$$\n\nLet $a$ be the side of the pentagon. We know that our polygons have equal perimeters. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =5a \\\\ 45 & =5a \\\\ 9 & =a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the length of the side is $9 \\,\\mathrm{cm}.$",
